    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$6^2+(-8)^2=36+64=100=10^2$, so $F$ lies on the circle.",
      "worked": "The circle has equation $x^2+y^2=100$.\n$$\\begin{align*}6^2+(-8)^2&=36+64\\\\6^2+(-8)^2&=100\\end{align*}$$\nThe coordinates satisfy the equation, so $F$ lies on the circle.",
